{"benchmark": "livebench_selected", "task_id": "paraphrase:f4cbfc58a683894a66b028420969bb75a35fe4acda1bd3dce0024062c11b2041", "sample_idx": 39, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "content": "\"To access the print version of the article, a link is provided. The rules for solving the Sudoku puzzle are outlined, with a key exception being that numbers within certain cells must sum up to specific figures located in the corners. This variation adds a new layer of complexity to the traditional puzzle. The standard rules still apply, such as not repeating numbers within each distinct shape formed by grey lines. The puzzle is a unique challenge that requires careful attention to detail and logical reasoning.\"\n\n\n \nAddition to the traditional Sudoku rules, the numbers contained within cells outlined by grey lines have a special condition. They must add up to the figures indicated in the corner of the puzzle. This means that solvers must not only focus on the individual rows, columns, and boxes but also consider the sums of numbers within these specially outlined areas. The constraint of not repeating numbers within each shape formed by grey lines remains in place, ensuring that the puzzle requires a combination of basic Sudoku skills and the ability to adapt to the new rule.\n\n\n \nThe completed puzzle can be found in next week’s Observer Digital Edition, providing a solution for those who are unable to solve it on their own. This allows readers to check their work or simply view the finished puzzle. The availability of the solution in a future edition gives solvers a deadline to work on the puzzle, adding an element of challenge and motivation. For those who enjoy Sudoku and are looking for a variation with an extra level of complexity, this puzzle is an intriguing option.\n\n\n \nSolving the puzzle requires a systematic approach, starting with the easiest clues and gradually working through the more difficult ones. As the solver fills in the numbers, they must constantly check for compliance with both the traditional Sudoku rules and the special condition regarding the sums of numbers within grey-lined cells. The process can be time-consuming but is also rewarding for those who enjoy logical puzzles and are looking for a challenge. The sense of accomplishment upon completing the puzzle is a significant part of its appeal.\n\n\n \nThe puzzle’s design, with its combination of traditional Sudoku rules and the added twist of summing numbers within grey-lined cells, offers a fresh and exciting challenge for puzzle enthusiasts. The requirement to not repeat numbers within each shape and to meet the sum conditions in the corners adds depth and complexity, making it a stimulating activity for the mind. Whether solving it as a form of entertainment or as a way to exercise logical reasoning skills, the puzzle provides an engaging and rewarding experience for those who take on the challenge.\"", "logprobs": [{"token": "\"To", "logprob": -0.4018803536891937}, {"token": " access", "logprob": -0.04305700585246086}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.0232519693672657}, {"token": " print", "logprob": -0.008725020103156567}, {"token": " version", "logprob": -7.486063259420916e-05}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.0031777145341038704}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.011118361726403236}, {"token": " article", "logprob": -0.2270030528306961}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.002512990264222026}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.024781323969364166}, {"token": " link", "logprob": -0.008299149572849274}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.0067192567512393}, {"token": " provided", "logprob": -0.00012361239350866526}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -0.31154054403305054}, {"token": " The", "logprob": -0.0039595551788806915}, {"token": " rules", "logprob": -0.11019902676343918}, {"token": " for", "logprob": -0.02659463882446289}, {"token": " solving", "logprob": -0.5781631469726562}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.03187396004796028}, {"token": " Sudoku", "logprob